      "message": "Do we have benchmarks to gauge the perf impact for these changes?  Adding a predicate and a branch will eat into (and could negate) whatever benefit we\u0027re getting from the fast path, so it would be interesting to compare against just the branchless/general impl below.\n\nIdeally, I think we should be able to evaluate uniformity upfront at pipeline build time, and use a separate specialized stage for the uniform case.  Then we\u0027d get the best of both worlds (fast path without branching or predicate penalty on every iteration).",
